{
  "_comment": [
    "Restart on adoption (owner, 2026-10-31 and 2026-11-01): the vectors of launch_verdict, the helper's answer to",
    "'was the player this connection reaches launched by THIS build?' -- current, older or unknown. Python only:",
    "the verdict lives only in the helper (the model mirrors the marker, never the reading). Run by",
    "tests/test_player_launch.py, each case against a REAL process whose /proc/<pid>/cmdline is the case's argv",
    "behind a holder script (everything before the socket token is ignored, so the holder's own two elements",
    "change nothing).",
    "Placeholders: __SOCK__ the test's socket, __RUNTIME__ its folder, __STATE__ the test's state folder.",
    "`tail: current` is THIS build's composed argv less its program name (mpv_launch_argv, both forms by",
    "`include`), never a literal: every part edit changes the build and so the marker. `older` shapes are each",
    "tag's OWN mpv_launch_argv, composed by that tag's helper and never by the verdict under test (design 17.8),",
    "generated once by",
    "  git archive <tag> bin manifest.json | tar -x -C <dir>",
    "then exec of <dir>/bin/omarchy-iptv into a namespace and",
    "  mpv_launch_argv('/run/user/1000/omarchy-iptv/mpv.sock', TOKENS, player_dirs(that, '/home/u/.local/state/omarchy-iptv'))",
    "with TOKENS [] for v0.16.0 and ['--osd-duration=4321'] (an inert canary) for v0.16.0-include and v0.15.0,",
    "the concrete paths replaced by the placeholders. v0.15.0 carries the canary ON its argv (before D-SINK-47).",
    "`edit`: replace (an element by its prefix, the new element), drop (an element), append (elements); a shape case",
    "takes an edit too. The placeholders are filled in an edit's elements as well.",
    "D-PLY-61 (lane-sk72, 2026-11-02, the lead's decision): elements APPENDED after this build's whole composition are",
    "the user's `mpv` wrapper (`exec /usr/bin/mpv \"$@\" --hwdec=auto`) and read current -- no older build can produce",
    "the prefix, whose marker carries the version and the part table's CRC -- except a second socket option, in any",
    "spelling, which re-points the element the verdict is anchored on and reads older. A difference INSIDE the",
    "composition, appended tokens or not, stays older."
  ],
